==Strategy==
The majority of this stage's difficulty comes in the swarm of enemies that appear upon hitting the base. The fortunate part about this swarm is that the Celeboodles drop huge amounts of money, meaning building up a large stack of attackers is very easy. Once the base hit wave is taken out, the stage is all but won. Do be careful, though; hitting deploy limit gives Miss Haka, Zir Zeal and Zory free reign to pummel your base.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime/Jelly Dumpling]] - Slime's waves can wipe entire swarms of enemies off the field, as well as deal some chip damage to the Dober. Be sure to time them carefully, as every missed slime attack can be very detrimental and allow the enemies to stack up quickly.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] - Cyborg, who is usually hardly serviceable due to her high cost, is the perfect unit for this stage. The presence of many Celeboodles means consistent cash, allowing Cyborg to be spammed for maximum effect. Accumulating Cyborgs will quickly destroy the Dober and the supporting traitless enemies, so long as you defend her from burrowing zombie enemies.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] - Cadaver Bear is great for dealing with Haka and the other zombies in the stage. If the player consistently spams Cadaver BearCat, Haka will constantly be pushed back and nuked by BearCat's high dph. When fighting the other zombies, however, be careful, as BearCat does not outrange them.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] - Housewife is great for both threats of the stage. Her high damage and long-distance means she's great for dealing with the traitless swarm, and her Zombie Killer allows her to dispatch of the Zories and Zeals quite easily. Be warned of her relatively long cooldown and low health, however; she won't be able to serve as a primary damage dealer unless the player defends and accumulates her well.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]] - An incredible unit for this stage if you have him. His immunity to waves and massive damage to enemies can quickly dispatch the Celebrodles and Dagshaunds in higher difficulties. However, you need to really watch out from the zombies, otherwise, a lot of money will be wasted.

